- Retained cash above the minimum liquidity reserve;
- Customer deposits, prepayments, minimum-volume commitments, or take-or-pay contracts;
- Vendor financing, equipment payment terms, landlord contributions, grants, or tax incentives;
- Working-capital improvements that do not damage supplier or customer relationships.

